<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mamikonian dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mamikonian family</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mamikonian family was one of the most powerful noble houses of ancient and early medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>, holding the hereditary office of commander-in-chief (sparapet) under the Arsacid kings. Its members led the Armenian defence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> against Sasanian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>, most famously <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vardan-mamikonian">Vardan Mamikonian</a>, killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-avarayr">Battle of Avarayr</a> in 451. The family declined after failed revolts against Arab rule in the 8th century.</p></div>
